{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f65ddc15","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005153,"end_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:47.021017+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:47.015864+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Refinement patch notes — six safeguards (not rerun)\n","\n","1. Mandatory Stage-1 availability/coverage gate before any training: only the first\n","   `np.array_split(B1, B1_SUBFOLDS)[0]` seed slice is exempt. Later B1 slices,\n","   B2–B4 and sealed OOT require finite [0,1] original scores. Availability,\n","   missingness and source metadata prevent prior-filled scores concealing gaps.\n","   Required/exempt counts and scope are logged and recorded.\n","2. All existing card/device/null-card audits explicitly use configured sample,\n","   lookback and deterministic context-specific seeds; actual checked-node counts\n","   are recorded, including B1 and frozen OOT. Extractors/null generators use the\n","   same configured lookback. The graph tie policy is unchanged; no new null-device\n","   audit is added.\n","3. Both upstream joins reject null/duplicate IDs, validate many-to-one cardinality\n","   and preserve left row count, index and ID order. Integrity errors propagate.\n","4. `stage_exit_decision` fails closed unless exactly one internal confirmatory\n","   **H2a Message Passing (Real - NoGraph)** at **pooled_dev (B2-B4)** has finite\n","   `delta_AP >= ACCEPTANCE_DELTA` and existing `p_adj <= FDR_ALPHA`. No mean AP,\n","   historical delta, shift diagnostic or OOT signal is used to advance/tune.\n","5. Before OOF export, assertions check Boolean flags, raw/calibrated missingness,\n","   finite valid probabilities, exact existing seed-prior filling and row-level\n","   provenance. Thin skipped B1 subfolds receive explicit unscored provenance.\n","   Disabled calibrated export is all NaN; internal calibration remains checked.\n","6. Streaming SHA-256 captures actual resolved input bytes when loaded: transaction,\n","   optional identity, ledger, Stage-1/optional Stage-2 OOF and optional Stage-2\n","   results. Missing optional files are recorded without fabricated hashes.\n","   `script_sha256` hashes actual `__file__`, otherwise is null with reason.\n","   Notebook code hash deterministically hashes UTF-8 JSON of IPython\n","   `input_hist_raw[1:]` at reporting (including that input), with\n","   `ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',', ':')`; outputs/metadata are excluded.\n","   Use a fresh kernel Run All for the published code-cell scope; manual inputs\n","   and reruns deliberately alter the fingerprint. No self-referential hash is embedded.\n","\n","Architecture, hyperparameters, temporal splits, training/calibration and prior-fill\n","policy are unchanged. All stale outputs, execution counts and run metadata are\n","cleared. **No training was rerun:** raw data/upstream run artifacts are not attached.\n","Static compilation and extracted-function toy tests are not model validation.\n","\n","**Known limitation deliberately unchanged:** the existing pooled B2–B4 bootstrap\n","includes full blocks despite its embargo docstring. The exit gate faithfully uses\n","that existing confirmatory result; this patch does not correct its pooled scope.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"57331a5b","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-01T03:13:47.03052Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-01T03:13:47.030101Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-01T03:13:52.949194Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-01T03:13:52.94853Z"},"papermill":{"duration":5.92597,"end_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:52.951097+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:47.025127+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["\"\"\"\n","Stage 3: Frozen Two-Stage Res-GNN Pipeline\n","==========================================\n","(Audit-Hardened Edition, v2 — protocol-aligned with Stage 1 v2 and Stage 2 v2)\n","\n","Purpose\n","-------\n","(a) Test whether time-causal message passing over entity graphs adds signal over\n","    an identical network with propagation disabled, under a temporally honest\n","    protocol; and\n","(b) emit a leakage-free `stage3_prob` representation with full block coverage,\n","    including the sealed OOT block, for the final joint-model comparison.\n","\n","Changes vs. Stage 3 v1 (and why each matters)\n","---------------------------------------------\n"," 1. THE PIPELINE WAS NEVER TWO-STAGE. v1 logged\n","       \"Tabular logit coverage: train 0.0%, val 0.0%\"\n","    on every fold — the Stage-1 artifact never resolved, so the `stage1_logit`\n","    node feature was a CONSTANT prior fallback and its availability flag was\n","    constantly 0. The architecture's defining input was inert. The loader is now\n","    schema-tolerant (Stage 1 v2 `stage1_prob_raw` / legacy `stage1_oof_prob`)\n","    and a missing artifact or unexpected coverage gap blocks training.\n"," 2. BLOCK 1 OOF EARLY-STOPPED ON ITS OWN TRAINING SET. v1 called\n","       train_and_predict(Z_b1_early, agg_fit, y_early,   # fit\n","                         Z_b1_early, agg_fit, y_early,   # \"stopping\" — SAME DATA\n","                         ...)\n","    so epoch selection maximised training-set AP. It duly ran to the epoch cap\n","    (20/20, inner AP 0.5021). Replaced by expanding chronological sub-folds\n","    (K=4), each with its own disjoint, time-ordered inner-stopping slice.\n"," 3. SINGLE-SEED COMPARISONS ON A NEURAL MODEL. v1 drew confirmatory conclusions\n","    from one seed per variant while the observed effects were ~0.008 AP —\n","    plausibly inside seed noise. Every variant now trains N_SEEDS models; the\n","    reported score is the seed-mean probability, and the per-seed AP standard\n","    deviation is printed next to each hypothesis delta so the reader can see\n","    whether the effect clears the noise floor.\n"," 4. EVALUATION and FEATURE-GENERATION separated (as in Stages 1-2 v2). Embargo\n","    applies to reported metrics only; the full block is scored for downstream\n","    coverage. Causality is enforced by assertion, not by the embargo.\n"," 5. BLOCK 5 IS NOW SCORED by a frozen model fit on Blocks 1-4. v1 left the OOT\n","    block with zero Stage-3 coverage, making the final joint comparison\n","    impossible. The Block 5 target is never read; enforced by assertion.\n"," 6. PREDECESSOR CAUSALITY IS ASSERTED, not assumed. Every extracted edge is\n","    checked for strict antecedence (t_pred < t_node) and lookback compliance on\n","    a random audit sample. v1 asserted nothing.\n"," 7. MULTIPLICITY CONTROL. Benjamini-Hochberg FDR across the confirmatory family\n","    (H2a, N2), with two-sided bootstrap p-values. Cross-run comparisons against\n","    Stage 1 / Stage 2 artifacts are demoted to EXPLORATORY and excluded from the\n","    family — they confound model family with run configuration.\n"," 8. CALIBRATION. Focal loss is deliberately miscalibrating; v1's ECE of\n","    0.085-0.107 (vs ~0.013 for the Stage-1 GBDT) is why its cost-rule loss was\n","    ~$630k against Stage 1's ~$437k. Isotonic calibration is now fit on the\n","    inner-stopping slice and both raw and calibrated scores are exported. The\n","    Bayes threshold rule is only meaningful on calibrated probabilities.\n"," 9. REPRESENTATION SHIFT IS ACTED ON. v1 printed a WARNING on all three folds\n","    (max |mean diff| 3.73 / 2.36 / 1.47) and proceeded silently. Shift is now\n","    recorded per fold, escalated against a configurable tolerance, and surfaced\n","    in the diagnostics table and manifest.\n","10. VECTORISED NEIGHBOUR AGGREGATION. v1 looped over ~590k nodes in Python per\n","    variant per fold. Replaced with a segment-sum (np.add.reduceat) formulation;\n","    a unit check against the naive loop is included.\n","11. torch.cuda.amp.* -> torch.amp.* (v1 emitted FutureWarning on every batch),\n","    with a version-safe fallback shim.\n","12. `slice_aggs` was defined inside the fold loop and then used after it — it\n","    survived on Python scope leakage. Now module scope.\n","13. BUG FIX: the Stage-2 AP log line used doubled braces and printed the literal\n","    dict-comprehension source text rather than the values (same defect as\n","    Stage 2 v1).\n","14. Recall@0.1%FPR promoted into the printed report (computed but never shown in\n","    v1, despite being the headline operating point), plus Loss_no_model floor,\n","    quantile-binned ECE, entity-overlap audit and determinism flags.\n","\n","Retained protocol invariants\n","----------------------------\n","  - Equal-row deterministic chronological blocks; 1-4 dev, 5 sealed OOT.\n","  - 1-day boundary embargo on all REPORTED validation metrics.\n","  - Inner-split (last 20% by time) early stopping; never the reported block.\n","  - Scalers / PCA / calibrators fitted strictly on training-window data.\n","  - Directed causal predecessors within a 30-day lookback.\n","  - Paired bootstrap CIs on AP deltas.\n","\"\"\"\n","\n","from __future__ import annotations\n","\n","import copy\n","import gc\n","import hashlib\n","import json\n","import os\n","import random\n","import warnings\n","from collections import deque\n","from datetime import datetime, timezone\n","\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import torch\n","import torch.nn as nn\n","import torch.nn.functional as F\n","from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n","from sklearn.isotonic import IsotonicRegression\n","from sklearn.metrics import average_precision_score, roc_auc_score\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n","from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, TensorDataset\n","\n","warnings.simplefilter(\"default\")\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=UserWarning, module=\"torch\")\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\n","    \"ignore\",\n","    category=DeprecationWarning,\n","    message=r\"datetime\\.datetime\\.utcnow\\(\\) is deprecated.*\",\n",")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"67e01948","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-01T03:13:52.962184Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-01T03:13:52.961689Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.239806Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.239199Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.285515,"end_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.241448+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:52.955933+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 1. Configuration\n","# ==============================================================================\n","CONFIG = {\n","    # --- Reproducibility & Schema ---\n","    \"SEED\": 42,\n","    \"N_SEEDS\": 3,                        # Neural runs per variant (see change #3)\n","    \"TIME_COLUMN\": \"TransactionDT\",\n","    \"TARGET_COLUMN\": \"isFraud\",\n","    \"ID_COLUMN\": \"TransactionID\",\n","    \"AMOUNT_COLUMN\": \"TransactionAmt\",\n","\n","    # --- Temporal Protocol & Embargo ---\n","    \"N_BLOCKS\": 5,\n","    \"DEV_BLOCKS\": [1, 2, 3, 4],\n","    \"OOT_BLOCK\": 5,\n","    \"SECONDS_PER_DAY\": 86_400,\n","    \"EMBARGO_SECONDS\": 86_400,\n","    \"LOOKBACK_WINDOW_SECS\": 30 * 86_400,\n","\n","    # EMBARGO SEMANTICS — identical to Stages 1-2 v2.\n","    # The embargo de-biases *reported* metrics. Causality is guaranteed by\n","    # train_max_dt <= score_min_dt assertions and by strict predecessor\n","    # antecedence, not by the embargo. The feature pass therefore scores the\n","    # full block for complete downstream coverage.\n","    \"EMBARGO_IN_FEATURE_PASS\": False,\n","\n","    # --- Early Stopping & Validation Integrity ---\n","    \"INNER_VAL_FRAC\": 0.20,\n","    \"MIN_STOP_ROWS\": 5_000,\n","    \"MIN_STOP_POSITIVES\": 50,\n","\n","    # --- Block 1 OOF sub-fold scheme ---\n","    \"B1_SUBFOLDS\": 4,                    # coverage (K-1)/K = 75% vs v1's 50%\n","\n","    # --- Calibration ---\n","    \"CALIBRATION\": \"isotonic\",           # {\"isotonic\", \"none\"}\n","    \"EXPORT_CALIBRATED_OOF\": True,\n","\n","    # --- Cost Model (Bayes-Optimal Decision Boundary) ---\n","    \"C_REVIEW\": 10.0,\n","    \"C_FRICTION\": 25.0,\n","\n","    # --- Operational Triage & Bootstrap ---\n","    \"INVESTIGATION_CAPACITY\": 0.01,\n","    \"N_BOOTSTRAP\": 400,\n","    \"BOOTSTRAP_ALPHA\": 0.05,\n","    \"ACCEPTANCE_DELTA\": 0.005,\n","    \"FDR_ALPHA\": 0.05,\n","\n","    # --- Neural Network & Graph Hyperparameters ---\n","    \"MAX_EPOCHS\": 20,\n","    \"PATIENCE\": 4,\n","    \"BATCH_SIZE\": 4096,\n","    \"HIDDEN_DIM\": 64,\n","    \"DROPOUT\": 0.20,\n","    \"LR\": 3e-3,\n","    \"WEIGHT_DECAY\": 1e-4,\n","    \"N_PCA\": 15,\n","    \"CARD_MAX_NEIGHBORS\": 10,\n","    \"DEVICE_MAX_NEIGHBORS\": 5,\n","    \"FOCAL_ALPHA\": 0.25,\n","    \"FOCAL_GAMMA\": 2.0,\n","\n","    # --- Diagnostics ---\n","    \"SHIFT_TOLERANCE\": 0.75,             # |mean diff| per standardised dim\n","    \"SHIFT_FAIL_HARD\": False,            # True -> raise instead of warn\n","    \"PREDECESSOR_AUDIT_SAMPLE\": 20_000,  # rows sampled for causality assertion\n","\n","    # --- Experimental Controls ---\n","    \"RUN_NULL_CONTROL\": True,            # N2: time-matched predecessors\n","    \"RUN_NO_GRAPH_ABLATION\": True,       # H2a: propagation disabled\n","\n","    # --- Search Paths ---\n","    \"CANDIDATE_DATA_DIRS\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/competitions/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","        \"./data/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","        \"./data\",\n","        \".\",\n","    ],\n","    \"CANDIDATE_DECISION_PATHS\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit/artifacts/feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/feature_decisions.csv\",\n","        \"feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"feature_decisions.csv\",\n","    ],\n","    \"CANDIDATE_STAGE1_OOF\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/fork-of-stage-1-standalone-tabular-lightgbm-basel/artifacts/stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-1-standalone-tabular-lightgbm-baseline/artifacts/stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-1-standalone-tabular-lightgbm-baseline/stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","    ],\n","    \"CANDIDATE_STAGE2_RESULTS\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/fork-of-stage-2-graph-augmented-gbdt-relational/artifacts/stage2_fold_results.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-2-graph-augmented-gbdt-relational-feature/artifacts/stage2_fold_results.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-2-graph-augmented-gbdt-relational-feature/stage2_fold_results.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/stage2_fold_results.csv\",\n","        \"stage2_fold_results.csv\",\n","    ],\n","    \"CANDIDATE_STAGE2_OOF\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/fork-of-stage-2-graph-augmented-gbdt-relational/artifacts/stage2_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-2-graph-augmented-gbdt-relational-feature/artifacts/stage2_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-2-graph-augmented-gbdt-relational-feature/stage2_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/stage2_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"stage2_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","    ],\n","    \"OUTPUT_DIR\": \"./artifacts\",\n","\n","    \"STRICT_TIME_CAUSALITY\": True,\n","    \"REPORT_TIE_DIAGNOSTICS\": True,\n","}\n","\n","TARGET_LEAKAGE_COLUMNS = [\n","    \"isFraud\",\n","    \"TransactionID\",\n","    \"TransactionDT\",\n","    \"elapsed_days\",\n","    \"day_index\",\n","    \"chrono_block\",\n","]\n","AUDIT_ONLY_COLUMNS = [\n","    \"uid_card\", \"uid_device\", \"card_first_seen\", \"device_first_seen\",\n","    \"stage1_prob_raw\", \"stage1_prob_calibrated\", \"stage1_prob_filled\",\n","    \"stage1_available\", \"stage1_missing\", \"stage1_source\", \"stage1_oof_prob\",\n","    \"stage2_prob_raw\", \"stage2_prob_calibrated\", \"stage2_prob_filled\",\n","    \"stage2_available\", \"stage2_missing\", \"stage2_source\", \"stage2_oof_prob\",\n","]\n","\n","DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n","os.makedirs(CONFIG[\"OUTPUT_DIR\"], exist_ok=True)\n","\n","\n","def set_global_seed(seed: int) -> None:\n","    \"\"\"Seed every RNG that can influence a training run.\"\"\"\n","    random.seed(seed)\n","    np.random.seed(seed)\n","    torch.manual_seed(seed)\n","    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n","        torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(seed)\n","    torch.backends.cudnn.deterministic = True\n","    torch.backends.cudnn.benchmark = False\n","\n","\n","set_global_seed(CONFIG[\"SEED\"])\n","\n","\n","# --- torch.amp version shim (v1 used the deprecated torch.cuda.amp.*) ---\n","def make_grad_scaler(enabled: bool):\n","    \"\"\"GradScaler across torch versions.\"\"\"\n","    try:\n","        return torch.amp.GradScaler(\"cuda\", enabled=enabled)\n","    except (AttributeError, TypeError):\n","        return torch.cuda.amp.GradScaler(enabled=enabled)\n","\n","\n","def autocast_ctx(enabled: bool):\n","    \"\"\"autocast context across torch versions.\"\"\"\n","    try:\n","        return torch.amp.autocast(\"cuda\", enabled=enabled)\n","    except (AttributeError, TypeError):\n","        return torch.cuda.amp.autocast(enabled=enabled)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"470d2faa","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.251418Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.250909Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.288953Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.288164Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.045098,"end_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.290592+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.245494+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 2. Shared Utilities (protocol-identical to Stages 1-2 v2)\n","# ==============================================================================\n","\n","def sha256_file(path: str, chunk_size: int = 1 << 20) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Streaming SHA-256 of the exact bytes at the resolved input path.\"\"\"\n","    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n","    with open(path, \"rb\") as handle:\n","        for chunk in iter(lambda: handle.read(chunk_size), b\"\"):\n","            digest.update(chunk)\n","    return digest.hexdigest()\n","\n","\n","input_artifacts: dict[str, dict] = {}\n","upstream_availability: dict[str, np.ndarray] = {}\n","predecessor_audits: list[dict] = []\n","\n","\n","def record_input_artifact(name: str, path: str | None, optional: bool = False) -> None:\n","    \"\"\"Capture input bytes when loaded, not a guessed candidate or output hash.\"\"\"\n","    resolved = os.path.realpath(path) if path is not None else None\n","    exists = resolved is not None and os.path.isfile(resolved)\n","    input_artifacts[name] = {\n","        \"resolved_path\": resolved, \"optional\": optional,\n","        \"status\": \"loaded\" if exists else \"missing\",\n","        \"sha256\": sha256_file(resolved) if exists else None,\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def code_fingerprints() -> dict:\n","    \"\"\"Notebook hash: deterministic JSON of IPython raw inputs, including this cell.\n","\n","    Scope is this kernel's executed raw input history (not outputs or notebook\n","    metadata). A clean Run All includes the published code cells in order;\n","    manual inputs/reruns change the scope and therefore the fingerprint.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    script_path = globals().get(\"__file__\")\n","    script_exists = bool(script_path and os.path.isfile(script_path))\n","    result = {\n","        \"script_sha256\": sha256_file(script_path) if script_exists else None,\n","        \"script_resolved_path\": os.path.realpath(script_path) if script_exists else None,\n","        \"script_sha256_reason\": None if script_exists else \"__file__ absent or not a file\",\n","        \"notebook_code_sha256\": None,\n","        \"notebook_code_sha256_scope\": \"IPython input_hist_raw[1:] at reporting; \"\n","            \"UTF-8 JSON array, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',', ':'); \"\n","            \"outputs/metadata excluded; includes current input and any manual inputs/reruns\",\n","    }\n","    try:\n","        history = list(get_ipython().history_manager.input_hist_raw[1:])\n","        if not history or not all(isinstance(code, str) for code in history):\n","            raise ValueError(\"no usable raw input history\")\n","        canonical = json.dumps(history, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode(\"utf-8\")\n","        result[\"notebook_code_sha256\"] = hashlib.sha256(canonical).hexdigest()\n","        result[\"notebook_code_input_count\"] = len(history)\n","    except (NameError, AttributeError, ValueError) as exc:\n","        result[\"notebook_code_sha256_reason\"] = str(exc)\n","    return result\n","\n","\n","def resolve_path(candidates: list[str], target_file: str | None = None) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Resolve the first existing directory (or dir/target_file) from candidates.\"\"\"\n","    for path in candidates:\n","        check_path = os.path.join(path, target_file) if target_file else path\n","        if os.path.exists(check_path):\n","            return check_path if target_file else path\n","    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Target {target_file or 'directory'} not found in {candidates}.\")\n","\n","\n","def resolve_first_existing(candidates: list[str]) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Return the first candidate file path that exists.\"\"\"\n","    for path in candidates:\n","        if os.path.exists(path):\n","            return path\n","    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"None of these paths exist: {candidates}\")\n","\n","\n","def reduce_memory(frame: pd.DataFrame, label: str = \"\") -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Downcast numeric columns to shrink the working set without value loss.\"\"\"\n","    before = frame.memory_usage(deep=False).sum() / 1024 ** 2\n","    for col in frame.columns:\n","        kind = frame[col].dtype.kind\n","        if kind == \"i\":\n","            frame[col] = pd.to_numeric(frame[col], downcast=\"integer\")\n","        elif kind == \"f\":\n","            frame[col] = frame[col].astype(np.float32)\n","    after = frame.memory_usage(deep=False).sum() / 1024 ** 2\n","    saved = (before - after) / max(before, 1e-9)\n","    print(f\"    Memory downcast{(' [' + label + ']') if label else ''}: \"\n","          f\"{before:.1f} MB -> {after:.1f} MB ({saved:.1%} saved)\")\n","    return frame\n","\n","\n","def create_temporal_blocks(frame: pd.DataFrame, n_blocks: int,\n","                           time_col: str = \"TransactionDT\",\n","                           id_col: str = \"TransactionID\") -> pd.Series:\n","    \"\"\"Assign equal-row-count chronological block labels 1..n_blocks deterministically.\"\"\"\n","    order = frame.sort_values([time_col, id_col], kind=\"mergesort\").index\n","    position = pd.Series(np.arange(len(order)), index=order)\n","    labels = np.minimum((position.values * n_blocks) // len(order), n_blocks - 1) + 1\n","    return pd.Series(labels.astype(np.int16), index=order).reindex(frame.index)\n","\n","\n","def alert_threshold(amounts: np.ndarray,\n","                    c_rev: float = CONFIG[\"C_REVIEW\"],\n","                    c_fric: float = CONFIG[\"C_FRICTION\"]) -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"Bayes-optimal per-transaction alert threshold p* = (C_rev+C_fric)/(Amt+C_fric).\"\"\"\n","    amounts_arr = np.asarray(amounts, dtype=float)\n","    return np.minimum((c_rev + c_fric) / (amounts_arr + c_fric), 1.0)\n","\n","\n","def expected_calibration_error(y_true: np.ndarray, y_prob: np.ndarray,\n","                               n_bins: int = 20, strategy: str = \"uniform\") -> float:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Bin-weighted ECE. Report BOTH strategies.\n","\n","    'uniform'  : equal-width bins. At ~3.5% prevalence the [0,0.05) bin holds\n","                 ~95% of the mass, so this statistic flatters every model.\n","    'quantile' : equal-frequency bins — far more discriminating in the\n","                 operationally relevant high-score region.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    y_true_arr = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=float)\n","    y_prob_arr = np.clip(np.asarray(y_prob, dtype=float), 0.0, 1.0)\n","    n = len(y_true_arr)\n","    if n == 0:\n","        return float(\"nan\")\n","\n","    if strategy == \"quantile\":\n","        edges = np.unique(np.quantile(y_prob_arr, np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1)))\n","        if len(edges) < 3:\n","            return expected_calibration_error(y_true_arr, y_prob_arr, n_bins, \"uniform\")\n","        bin_idx = np.clip(np.digitize(y_prob_arr, edges[1:-1], right=False), 0, len(edges) - 2)\n","        n_eff = len(edges) - 1\n","    else:\n","        edges = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1)\n","        bin_idx = np.clip(np.digitize(y_prob_arr, edges[1:-1], right=False), 0, n_bins - 1)\n","        n_eff = n_bins\n","\n","    total_error = 0.0\n","    for b in range(n_eff):\n","        mask = bin_idx == b\n","        count = int(mask.sum())\n","        if count > 0:\n","            total_error += count * abs(y_prob_arr[mask].mean() - y_true_arr[mask].mean())\n","    return float(total_error / n)\n","\n","\n","def compute_metrics(y_true: np.ndarray, y_prob: np.ndarray, amounts: np.ndarray,\n","                    capacity: float = CONFIG[\"INVESTIGATION_CAPACITY\"]) -> dict[str, float]:\n","    \"\"\"Ranking, calibration, triage and economic metrics for one scored window.\"\"\"\n","    y_true = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=int)\n","    y_prob = np.asarray(y_prob, dtype=float)\n","    amounts = np.asarray(amounts, dtype=float)\n","\n","    ap = float(average_precision_score(y_true, y_prob))\n","    try:\n","        roc = float(roc_auc_score(y_true, y_prob))\n","    except ValueError:\n","        roc = float(\"nan\")\n","\n","    p_safe = np.clip(y_prob, 1e-15, 1.0 - 1e-15)\n","    log_loss = float(-np.mean(y_true * np.log(p_safe) + (1 - y_true) * np.log(1.0 - p_safe)))\n","    brier = float(np.mean((y_prob - y_true) ** 2))\n","    ece_u = expected_calibration_error(y_true, y_prob, 20, \"uniform\")\n","    ece_q = expected_calibration_error(y_true, y_prob, 20, \"quantile\")\n","\n","    order = np.lexsort((-amounts, -y_prob))\n","    y_sorted = y_true[order]\n","    n_neg = int((y_sorted == 0).sum())\n","    n_pos = int((y_sorted == 1).sum())\n","    cum_fp = (y_sorted == 0).cumsum()\n","\n","    def recall_at_fpr(target_fpr: float) -> float:\n","        budget = int(np.floor(target_fpr * n_neg))\n","        alerted_pos = int(y_sorted[cum_fp <= budget].sum())\n","        return float(alerted_pos / n_pos) if n_pos > 0 else 0.0\n","\n","    k_cap = max(1, int(np.floor(capacity * len(y_sorted))))\n","    prec_at_cap = float(y_sorted[:k_cap].mean())\n","    rec_at_cap = float(y_sorted[:k_cap].sum() / n_pos) if n_pos > 0 else 0.0\n","\n","    def financial_loss(predictions: np.ndarray) -> float:\n","        fn_mask = (y_true == 1) & (predictions == 0)\n","        fp_mask = (y_true == 0) & (predictions == 1)\n","        return float(amounts[fn_mask].sum()\n","                     + predictions.sum() * CONFIG[\"C_REVIEW\"]\n","                     + fp_mask.sum() * CONFIG[\"C_FRICTION\"])\n","\n","    preds_cost_rule = (y_prob > alert_threshold(amounts)).astype(int)\n","    preds_flat_half = (y_prob >= 0.5).astype(int)\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"AP\": ap,\n","        \"ROC_AUC\": roc,\n","        \"LogLoss\": log_loss,\n","        \"Brier\": brier,\n","        \"ECE\": ece_u,\n","        \"ECE_quantile\": ece_q,\n","        \"Recall@0.1%FPR\": recall_at_fpr(0.001),\n","        \"Recall@1.0%FPR\": recall_at_fpr(0.010),\n","        f\"Prec@{capacity:.1%}cap\": prec_at_cap,\n","        f\"Recall@{capacity:.1%}cap\": rec_at_cap,\n","        \"Loss_cost_rule\": financial_loss(preds_cost_rule),\n","        \"Loss_flat_0.5\": financial_loss(preds_flat_half),\n","        \"Loss_no_model\": float(amounts[y_true == 1].sum()),\n","        \"AlertRate\": float(preds_cost_rule.mean()),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def bootstrap_ap_delta(y_true: np.ndarray, p_new: np.ndarray, p_ref: np.ndarray,\n","                       n_boot: int = CONFIG[\"N_BOOTSTRAP\"],\n","                       alpha: float = CONFIG[\"BOOTSTRAP_ALPHA\"],\n","                       seed: int = CONFIG[\"SEED\"]) -> dict[str, float | int]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Paired bootstrap of AP(p_new) - AP(p_ref) over identical resampled rows.\n","\n","    Returns a two-sided bootstrap p-value alongside the CI so the confirmatory\n","    family can be FDR-corrected downstream.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    y_arr = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=int)\n","    p_new_arr = np.asarray(p_new, dtype=float)\n","    p_ref_arr = np.asarray(p_ref, dtype=float)\n","    n = len(y_arr)\n","\n","    observed = float(average_precision_score(y_arr, p_new_arr)\n","                     - average_precision_score(y_arr, p_ref_arr))\n","    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n","    deltas = np.empty(n_boot, dtype=float)\n","    valid = 0\n","    for _ in range(n_boot):\n","        idx = rng.integers(0, n, size=n)\n","        y_b = y_arr[idx]\n","        if y_b.sum() == 0 or y_b.sum() == n:\n","            continue\n","        deltas[valid] = (average_precision_score(y_b, p_new_arr[idx])\n","                         - average_precision_score(y_b, p_ref_arr[idx]))\n","        valid += 1\n","\n","    deltas = deltas[:valid]\n","    if valid == 0:\n","        return {\"delta\": observed, \"ci_low\": np.nan, \"ci_high\": np.nan,\n","                \"p_win\": np.nan, \"p_value\": np.nan, \"n_boot\": 0}\n","\n","    ci_low, ci_high = np.percentile(deltas, [100 * alpha / 2, 100 * (1.0 - alpha / 2)])\n","    p_win = float((deltas > 0.0).mean())\n","    p_two = float(min(1.0, max(2.0 * min(p_win, 1.0 - p_win), 1.0 / valid)))\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"delta\": observed,\n","        \"ci_low\": float(ci_low),\n","        \"ci_high\": float(ci_high),\n","        \"p_win\": p_win,\n","        \"p_value\": p_two,\n","        \"n_boot\": int(valid),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def benjamini_hochberg(p_values: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Benjamini-Hochberg FDR control.\n","\n","    Returns (reject_flags, adjusted_p_values). Required because the confirmatory\n","    family spans several hypotheses across largely overlapping rows; declaring\n","    each independently inflates the family-wise error rate.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    p = np.asarray(p_values, dtype=float)\n","    m = len(p)\n","    if m == 0:\n","        return np.array([], dtype=bool), np.array([], dtype=float)\n","\n","    order = np.argsort(p)\n","    ranked = p[order]\n","    adj_sorted = np.minimum.accumulate((ranked * m / np.arange(1, m + 1))[::-1])[::-1]\n","    adj_sorted = np.clip(adj_sorted, 0.0, 1.0)\n","\n","    adjusted = np.empty(m, dtype=float)\n","    adjusted[order] = adj_sorted\n","    return adjusted <= alpha, adjusted\n","\n","\n","def build_entity_uids(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> tuple[pd.Series, pd.Series]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Registration-anchored entity proxies (graph keys and audit only).\n","\n","    Anchor = day_index - D1, an approximate account-open date. These strings are\n","    never model features — only graph adjacency keys.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    anchor = np.where(\n","        frame[\"D1\"].isna(),\n","        \"na\",\n","        (frame[\"day_index\"] - frame[\"D1\"].fillna(0)).astype(\"int64\").astype(str),\n","    )\n","\n","    def col_str(name: str, fill) -> pd.Series:\n","        if name not in frame.columns:\n","            return pd.Series([\"na\"] * len(frame), index=frame.index)\n","        return frame[name].fillna(fill).astype(str)\n","\n","    uid_card = (\n","        col_str(\"card1\", -1) + \"_\" + col_str(\"card2\", -1) + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"card3\", -1) + \"_\" + col_str(\"card4\", \"na\") + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"card5\", -1) + \"_\" + col_str(\"card6\", \"na\") + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"addr1\", -1) + \"_\" + pd.Series(anchor, index=frame.index)\n","    )\n","    uid_device = (\n","        col_str(\"DeviceInfo\", \"no_dev\") + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"id_30\", \"no_os\") + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"id_31\", \"no_brw\")\n","    )\n","    return uid_card, uid_device\n","\n","\n","def first_seen_flag(entity_series: pd.Series) -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"True on an entity's first chronological appearance (depends only on the past).\"\"\"\n","    return ~entity_series.duplicated(keep=\"first\").to_numpy()\n","\n","\n","def entity_overlap_rate(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, score_idx, col: str) -> float:\n","    \"\"\"Share of scored rows whose entity was already observed in the training window.\"\"\"\n","    seen = set(frame.loc[train_idx, col].unique())\n","    return float(frame.loc[score_idx, col].isin(seen).mean())\n","\n","\n","def assert_causal(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, score_idx, label: str,\n","                  time_col: str = CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]) -> None:\n","    \"\"\"Hard guarantee that every training row precedes (or ties) every scored row.\"\"\"\n","    if len(train_idx) == 0 or len(score_idx) == 0:\n","        return\n","    train_max = frame.loc[train_idx, time_col].max()\n","    score_min = frame.loc[score_idx, time_col].min()\n","    assert train_max <= score_min, (\n","        f\"CAUSALITY VIOLATION [{label}]: train_max_dt={train_max} > score_min_dt={score_min}\"\n","    )\n","\n","\n","def time_ordered_inner_split(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, frac: float,\n","                             time_col: str = CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]):\n","    \"\"\"Split a training index into (fit, stop) where stop is the latest `frac` by time.\"\"\"\n","    train_dt = frame.loc[train_idx, time_col].to_numpy()\n","    threshold = np.quantile(train_dt, 1.0 - frac)\n","    return train_idx[train_dt < threshold], train_idx[train_dt >= threshold]\n","\n","\n","def rows_positional_split(n_rows: int, dt: np.ndarray, frac: float) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Positional (fit, stop) split of an already chronologically-ordered array.\n","\n","    Used inside the neural pipeline where arrays are positional rather than\n","    DataFrame-indexed. Returns boolean masks.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    threshold = np.quantile(dt, 1.0 - frac)\n","    fit_mask = dt < threshold\n","    stop_mask = ~fit_mask\n","    return fit_mask, stop_mask"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"41a50c9a","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.300125Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.299675Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.312281Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.31158Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.019145,"end_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.313582+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.294437+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 3. Neural Feature Pipeline\n","# ==============================================================================\n","LOG_COLS = [\"TransactionAmt\", \"dist1\", \"dist2\", \"C1\", \"C2\", \"C13\"]\n","\n","\n","def build_neural_features(df_fit: pd.DataFrame, df_apply: pd.DataFrame,\n","                          v_columns: list[str], num_columns: list[str],\n","                          n_pca: int = CONFIG[\"N_PCA\"],\n","                          prior: float | None = None) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, dict]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Build the aligned continuous node representation Z0.\n","\n","    Medians, StandardScaler and PCA are fitted strictly on `df_fit` (the training\n","    window) and merely applied to `df_apply`. The frozen Stage-1 probability is\n","    converted to a logit and paired with an explicit availability flag so the\n","    network can learn \"no upstream score\" as a distinct state rather than\n","    silently absorbing a constant.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    X_fit = df_fit[num_columns].copy()\n","    X_app = df_apply[num_columns].copy()\n","\n","    for col in LOG_COLS:\n","        if col in num_columns:\n","            X_fit[col] = np.log1p(np.maximum(0.0, X_fit[col].fillna(0.0)))\n","            X_app[col] = np.log1p(np.maximum(0.0, X_app[col].fillna(0.0)))\n","\n","    fill_values = X_fit.median().fillna(0.0)\n","\n","    scaler = StandardScaler()\n","    X_fit_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_fit.fillna(fill_values))\n","    X_app_scaled = scaler.transform(X_app.fillna(fill_values))\n","\n","    v_scaler = StandardScaler()\n","    V_fit = v_scaler.fit_transform(df_fit[v_columns].fillna(0.0))\n","    V_app = v_scaler.transform(df_apply[v_columns].fillna(0.0))\n","\n","    n_comp = int(min(n_pca, V_fit.shape[1], max(1, V_fit.shape[0] - 1)))\n","    pca = PCA(n_components=n_comp, svd_solver=\"randomized\", random_state=CONFIG[\"SEED\"])\n","    V_fit_pca = pca.fit_transform(V_fit)\n","    V_app_pca = pca.transform(V_app)\n","\n","    fit_prior = float(df_fit[CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]].mean()) if prior is None else prior\n","    eps = 1e-6\n","\n","    def to_logit(sub_frame: pd.DataFrame) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n","        raw_prob = (sub_frame[\"stage1_prob_raw\"]\n","                    if \"stage1_prob_raw\" in sub_frame.columns\n","                    else pd.Series(np.nan, index=sub_frame.index))\n","        avail = raw_prob.notna().to_numpy().astype(np.float32)\n","        p = np.clip(raw_prob.fillna(fit_prior).to_numpy(dtype=float), eps, 1.0 - eps)\n","        return np.log(p / (1.0 - p)).astype(np.float32), avail\n","\n","    logit_fit, avail_fit = to_logit(df_fit)\n","    logit_app, avail_app = to_logit(df_apply)\n","\n","    Z_fit = np.hstack([X_fit_scaled, V_fit_pca,\n","                       logit_fit.reshape(-1, 1), avail_fit.reshape(-1, 1)]).astype(np.float32)\n","    Z_app = np.hstack([X_app_scaled, V_app_pca,\n","                       logit_app.reshape(-1, 1), avail_app.reshape(-1, 1)]).astype(np.float32)\n","\n","    assert np.isfinite(Z_fit).all(), \"Fatal: non-finite values in Z_fit.\"\n","    assert np.isfinite(Z_app).all(), \"Fatal: non-finite values in Z_app.\"\n","\n","    info = {\n","        \"pca_components\": n_comp,\n","        \"pca_explained\": float(pca.explained_variance_ratio_.sum()),\n","        \"avail_fit\": float(avail_fit.mean()),\n","        \"avail_app\": float(avail_app.mean()),\n","    }\n","    return Z_fit, Z_app, info\n","\n","\n","def check_representation_shift(Z_fit: np.ndarray, Z_app: np.ndarray, label: str = \"val\",\n","                               tol: float = CONFIG[\"SHIFT_TOLERANCE\"],\n","                               skip_tail: int = 2) -> dict:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Detect covariate shift between the fitted and applied embedding spaces.\n","\n","    The last `skip_tail` dims are the Stage-1 logit and its availability flag,\n","    which are expected to shift and are excluded. v1 printed this and moved on;\n","    the result is now recorded and optionally escalated.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    n_dim = Z_fit.shape[1] - skip_tail\n","    shift = np.abs(Z_app[:, :n_dim].mean(axis=0) - Z_fit[:, :n_dim].mean(axis=0))\n","    worst = float(shift.max())\n","    n_bad = int((shift > tol).sum())\n","    status = \"OK\" if n_bad == 0 else \"WARNING\"\n","    print(f\"    [{status}] Representation shift ({label}): max |mean diff| {worst:.3f} \"\n","          f\"across {n_dim} dims | {n_bad} dim(s) > {tol}\")\n","    if n_bad > 0 and CONFIG[\"SHIFT_FAIL_HARD\"]:\n","        raise RuntimeError(f\"Representation shift exceeded tolerance in {label}.\")\n","    return {\"max_shift\": worst, \"n_shifted_dims\": n_bad}"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"b8967ef2","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.322887Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.322371Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.344218Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.343486Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.028347,"end_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.345765+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.317418+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 4. Time-Causal Graph Construction\n","# ==============================================================================\n","def extract_causal_predecessors(\n","    transaction_dt: np.ndarray,\n","    entity_series: np.ndarray,\n","    max_neighbors: int = 10,\n","    lookback: int = 30 * 86_400,\n","    strict_time: bool = True,\n",") -> tuple[list[list[int]], dict]:\n","\n","    histories: dict[object, deque] = {}\n","    predecessors: list[list[int]] = []\n","    n_tie_skipped = 0\n","    n_nodes_with_ties = 0\n","\n","    for idx in range(len(transaction_dt)):\n","        dt = transaction_dt[idx]\n","        ent = entity_series[idx]\n","        h = histories.setdefault(ent, deque())\n","\n","        # Drop entries that have aged out of the lookback window.\n","        while h and (dt - h[0][0] > lookback):\n","            h.popleft()\n","\n","        # Reverse scan: most recent first. Deque is ascending in time and every\n","        # entry has a lower index, so `t_prev >= dt` can only mean a tie.\n","        selected: list[int] = []\n","        node_ties = 0\n","        for t_prev, j in reversed(h):\n","            if strict_time and t_prev >= dt:\n","                node_ties += 1\n","                continue                      # skip the tie, keep scanning back\n","            selected.append(j)\n","            if len(selected) >= max_neighbors:\n","                break\n","        selected.reverse()\n","\n","        if node_ties:\n","            n_tie_skipped += node_ties\n","            n_nodes_with_ties += 1\n","\n","        predecessors.append(selected)\n","        h.append((dt, idx))                   # insert AFTER reading\n","\n","    stats = {\n","        \"strict_time\": bool(strict_time),\n","        \"tie_edges_skipped\": int(n_tie_skipped),\n","        \"nodes_with_tie_neighbours\": int(n_nodes_with_ties),\n","        \"total_edges\": int(sum(len(p) for p in predecessors)),\n","    }\n","    return predecessors, stats\n","\n","\n","def audit_predecessor_causality(\n","    transaction_dt: np.ndarray,\n","    hist: list[list[int]],\n","    label: str,\n","    lookback: int = 30 * 86_400,\n","    sample: int = 20_000,\n","    seed: int = 42,\n","    strict_time: bool = True,\n",") -> dict:\n","\n","    n = len(hist)\n","    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n","    idx_pool = np.arange(n) if n <= sample else rng.choice(n, size=sample, replace=False)\n","\n","    n_edges = 0\n","    n_ties = 0\n","    for i in idx_pool:\n","        neigh = hist[i]\n","        if not neigh:\n","            continue\n","        arr = np.asarray(neigh, dtype=np.int64)\n","        n_edges += arr.size\n","\n","        assert (arr < i).all(), (\n","            f\"LEAKAGE [{label}]: nodee {i} references a non-prior index \"\n","            \"(score-before-insert ordering was violated).\"\n","        )\n","\n","        dts = transaction_dt[arr]\n","        assert (dts <= transaction_dt[i]).all(), (      # <= : future is always fatal\n","            f\"LEAKAGE [{label}]: node {i} references a FUTURE timestamp. \"\n","            \"The frame is not chronologically sorted.\"\n","        )\n","\n","        ties = int((dts == transaction_dt[i]).sum())\n","        if strict_time:\n","            assert ties == 0, (\n","                f\"LEAKAGE [{label}]: node {i} references {ties} same-timestamp \"\n","                \"neighbour(s) under STRICT_TIME_CAUSALITY. The extractor should \"\n","                \"have filtered these.\"\n","            )\n","        n_ties += ties\n","\n","        assert (transaction_dt[i] - dts <= lookback).all(), (\n","            f\"WINDOW VIOLATION [{label}]: node {i} references beyond the  lookback.\"\n","        )\n","\n","    mode = \"STRICT\" if strict_time else \"PERMISSIVE\"\n","    tie_note = \"\" if strict_time else f\" | {n_ties:,} tie-edges allowed\"\n","    print(f\"      causality audit [{label}]: PASSED ({mode}) \"\n","          f\"{len(idx_pool):,} nodes sampled (requested {sample:,}), \"\n","          f\"lookback={lookback}s, seed={seed}, {n_edges:,} edges checked{tie_note}\")\n","\n","    result = {\"label\": label, \"nodes_checked\": int(len(idx_pool)),\n","              \"requested_sample\": int(sample), \"lookback_seconds\": int(lookback),\n","              \"seed\": int(seed), \"edges_checked\": int(n_edges),\n","              \"tie_edges\": int(n_ties), \"mode\": mode}\n","    predecessor_audits.append(result)\n","    return result\n","\n","\n","def time_matched_null_predecessors(\n","    transaction_dt: np.ndarray,\n","    real_hist: list[list[int]],\n","    seed: int = 42,\n","    lookback: int = 30 * 86_400,\n","    strict_time: bool = True,\n",") -> list[list[int]]:\n","    \n","    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n","    dt = np.asarray(transaction_dt)\n","    n = len(dt)\n","\n","    # Start index of each row's tie group; equals i when its timestamp is unique.\n","    tie_start = (np.searchsorted(dt, dt, side=\"left\")\n","                 if strict_time else np.arange(n, dtype=np.int64))\n","\n","    lo = 0\n","    null_hist: list[list[int]] = []\n","    for i in range(n):\n","        while dt[i] - dt[lo] > lookback:\n","            lo += 1\n","        k = len(real_hist[i])\n","        hi = int(tie_start[i]) if strict_time else i     # cap below the tie group\n","        width = hi - lo\n","        if k == 0 or width <= 0:\n","            null_hist.append([])\n","        else:\n","            null_hist.append((lo + rng.integers(0, width, size=k)).tolist())\n","    return null_hist\n","\n","\n","def aggregate_neighbours(Z: np.ndarray, hist: list[list[int]]) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Mean of each node's predecessor representations, plus an active-edge mask.\n","\n","    Vectorised segment-sum formulation. v1 looped over every node in Python for\n","    every variant on every fold; this builds a flat (dst, src) edge list once and\n","    reduces it with np.add.reduceat.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    n, d = len(hist), Z.shape[1]\n","    agg = np.zeros((n, d), dtype=np.float32)\n","    mask = np.zeros((n, 1), dtype=np.float32)\n","\n","    counts = np.fromiter((len(h) for h in hist), dtype=np.int64, count=n)\n","    total = int(counts.sum())\n","    if total == 0:\n","        return agg, mask\n","\n","    src = np.empty(total, dtype=np.int64)\n","    pos = 0\n","    for h in hist:\n","        k = len(h)\n","        if k:\n","            src[pos:pos + k] = h\n","            pos += k\n","\n","    offsets = np.concatenate(([0], np.cumsum(counts)))\n","    valid = counts > 0\n","    # Empty segments have offsets[j] == offsets[j+1] and contribute no rows, so\n","    # reducing only at the valid starts yields exactly one sum per valid node.\n","    sums = np.add.reduceat(Z[src], offsets[:-1][valid], axis=0)\n","    agg[valid] = (sums / counts[valid, None]).astype(np.float32)\n","    mask[valid] = 1.0\n","    return agg, mask\n","\n","\n","def neighbour_means(Z: np.ndarray, card_hist: list[list[int]],\n","                    device_hist: list[list[int]]) -> tuple[np.ndarray, ...]:\n","    \"\"\"Card and device neighbourhood aggregates with their masks.\"\"\"\n","    card_agg, card_mask = aggregate_neighbours(Z, card_hist)\n","    dev_agg, dev_mask = aggregate_neighbours(Z, device_hist)\n","    return card_agg, card_mask, dev_agg, dev_mask\n","\n","\n","def blank_aggs(n: int, d: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, ...]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    H2a ablation: identical network, propagation disabled.\n","\n","    Masks are zeroed, so the card/device branches contribute nothing and the\n","    model reduces to an MLP over Z0. Parameter count is unchanged, so the\n","    comparison isolates message passing rather than capacity.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    return (\n","        np.zeros((n, d), dtype=np.float32),\n","        np.zeros((n, 1), dtype=np.float32),\n","        np.zeros((n, d), dtype=np.float32),\n","        np.zeros((n, 1), dtype=np.float32),\n","    )\n","\n","\n","def slice_aggs(agg_tuple: tuple[np.ndarray, ...], lo: int, hi: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, ...]:\n","    \"\"\"Positional slice of an aggregate tuple. (v1 defined this inside a loop.)\"\"\"\n","    return tuple(a[lo:hi] for a in agg_tuple)\n","\n","\n","def report_connectivity(card_mask: np.ndarray, dev_mask: np.ndarray, label: str) -> float:\n","    \"\"\"Proportion of nodes reachable by at least one message-passing edge.\"\"\"\n","    any_conn = float(((card_mask + dev_mask) > 0).mean())\n","    print(f\"    Connectivity ({label}): card {card_mask.mean():.1%} | \"\n","          f\"device {dev_mask.mean():.1%} | any {any_conn:.1%}\")\n","    return any_conn"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"10fd1826","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.355044Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.354792Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.37597Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.375371Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.027665,"end_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.377329+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.349664+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 5. Architecture, Loss, Training\n","# ==============================================================================\n","class FrozenResGNN(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Decoupled two-stage Res-GNN over frozen tabular inputs.\n","\n","    Self, card-neighbourhood and device-neighbourhood projections are fused, then\n","    concatenated with the raw node representation via a residual skip so the\n","    classifier retains direct access to Z0 even when the graph contributes\n","    nothing.\n","    \"\"\"\n","\n","    def __init__(self, in_dim: int, hidden_dim: int = 64, dropout: float = 0.2):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.proj_self = nn.Linear(in_dim, hidden_dim)\n","        self.proj_card = nn.Linear(in_dim, hidden_dim)\n","        self.proj_dev = nn.Linear(in_dim, hidden_dim)\n","        self.agg = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Linear(hidden_dim * 3, hidden_dim),\n","            nn.SELU(),\n","            nn.Dropout(dropout),\n","            nn.Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim),\n","            nn.SELU(),\n","        )\n","        self.classifier = nn.Linear(hidden_dim + in_dim, 1)\n","\n","    def forward(self, z: torch.Tensor, card_h: torch.Tensor, card_mask: torch.Tensor,\n","                dev_h: torch.Tensor, dev_mask: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n","        h_self = F.selu(self.proj_self(z))\n","        h_card = F.selu(self.proj_card(card_h)) * card_mask\n","        h_dev = F.selu(self.proj_dev(dev_h)) * dev_mask\n","        h_graph = self.agg(torch.cat([h_self, h_card, h_dev], dim=1))\n","        return self.classifier(torch.cat([h_graph, z], dim=1)).squeeze(1)\n","\n","\n","class FocalLoss(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Focal loss for extreme class imbalance.\n","\n","    NOTE: focal loss deliberately distorts the probability scale. Downstream\n","    isotonic calibration is therefore not optional — the Bayes cost rule is\n","    meaningless on raw focal outputs.\n","    \"\"\"\n","\n","    def __init__(self, alpha: float = 0.25, gamma: float = 2.0):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.alpha = alpha\n","        self.gamma = gamma\n","\n","    def forward(self, logits: torch.Tensor, targets: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n","        probs = torch.sigmoid(logits)\n","        bce = F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(logits, targets, reduction=\"none\")\n","        p_t = targets * probs + (1.0 - targets) * (1.0 - probs)\n","        alpha_t = targets * self.alpha + (1.0 - targets) * (1.0 - self.alpha)\n","        return (alpha_t * ((1.0 - p_t) ** self.gamma) * bce).mean()\n","\n","\n","@torch.no_grad()\n","def infer(model: nn.Module, Z: np.ndarray, agg: tuple[np.ndarray, ...],\n","          batch_size: int = 32768) -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"Batched sigmoid inference.\"\"\"\n","    model.eval()\n","    outputs = []\n","    for i in range(0, len(Z), batch_size):\n","        s = slice(i, i + batch_size)\n","        args = [torch.from_numpy(np.ascontiguousarray(Z[s])).to(DEVICE)]\n","        args += [torch.from_numpy(np.ascontiguousarray(a[s])).to(DEVICE) for a in agg]\n","        outputs.append(torch.sigmoid(model(*args)).float().cpu().numpy())\n","    return np.concatenate(outputs) if outputs else np.empty(0, dtype=np.float32)\n","\n","\n","def train_one_model(Z_fit, agg_fit, y_fit, Z_stop, agg_stop, y_stop,\n","                    seed: int, label: str = \"\"):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Train one FrozenResGNN with early stopping on a DISJOINT inner slice.\n","\n","    Returns (model, best_epoch, best_inner_ap). The caller is responsible for\n","    guaranteeing that (Z_stop, y_stop) is disjoint from (Z_fit, y_fit) — v1's\n","    Block-1 path passed the same arrays for both and selected epochs on\n","    training-set AP.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    assert len(Z_fit) > 0 and len(Z_stop) > 0, f\"[{label}] empty fit or stop slice.\"\n","    set_global_seed(seed)\n","\n","    model = FrozenResGNN(Z_fit.shape[1], CONFIG[\"HIDDEN_DIM\"], CONFIG[\"DROPOUT\"]).to(DEVICE)\n","    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=CONFIG[\"LR\"],\n","                                  weight_decay=CONFIG[\"WEIGHT_DECAY\"])\n","    criterion = FocalLoss(CONFIG[\"FOCAL_ALPHA\"], CONFIG[\"FOCAL_GAMMA\"])\n","    use_amp = DEVICE.type == \"cuda\"\n","    scaler_amp = make_grad_scaler(use_amp)\n","\n","    generator = torch.Generator()\n","    generator.manual_seed(seed)\n","    loader = DataLoader(\n","        TensorDataset(\n","            torch.from_numpy(np.ascontiguousarray(Z_fit)),\n","            *[torch.from_numpy(np.ascontiguousarray(a)) for a in agg_fit],\n","            torch.from_numpy(y_fit.astype(np.float32)),\n","        ),\n","        batch_size=CONFIG[\"BATCH_SIZE\"],\n","        shuffle=True,\n","        generator=generator,\n","        pin_memory=False,\n","    )\n","\n","    best_ap, best_state, best_epoch, stale = -np.inf, None, 0, 0\n","    for epoch in range(1, CONFIG[\"MAX_EPOCHS\"] + 1):\n","        model.train()\n","        for b_z, b_ca, b_cm, b_da, b_dm, b_y in loader:\n","            optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n","            with autocast_ctx(use_amp):\n","                logits = model(b_z.to(DEVICE), b_ca.to(DEVICE), b_cm.to(DEVICE),\n","                               b_da.to(DEVICE), b_dm.to(DEVICE))\n","                loss = criterion(logits, b_y.to(DEVICE))\n","            scaler_amp.scale(loss).backward()\n","            scaler_amp.step(optimizer)\n","            scaler_amp.update()\n","\n","        stop_probs = infer(model, Z_stop, agg_stop)\n","        current_ap = float(average_precision_score(y_stop, stop_probs))\n","        if current_ap > best_ap:\n","            best_ap, best_epoch, stale = current_ap, epoch, 0\n","            best_state = copy.deepcopy(model.state_dict())\n","        else:\n","            stale += 1\n","            if stale >= CONFIG[\"PATIENCE\"]:\n","                break\n","\n","    model.load_state_dict(best_state)\n","    return model, best_epoch, best_ap\n","\n","\n","def fit_calibrator(probs_stop: np.ndarray, y_stop: np.ndarray):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Isotonic calibration fit ONLY on the inner-stopping slice.\n","\n","    That slice is already spent for reporting, so it is the only honest\n","    calibration surface that does not touch the validation block.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if CONFIG[\"CALIBRATION\"] != \"isotonic\":\n","        return None\n","    if len(y_stop) == 0 or y_stop.sum() < CONFIG[\"MIN_STOP_POSITIVES\"]:\n","        return None\n","    iso = IsotonicRegression(y_min=0.0, y_max=1.0, out_of_bounds=\"clip\")\n","    iso.fit(probs_stop, y_stop)\n","    return iso\n","\n","\n","def apply_calibrator(calibrator, probs: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"Apply a fitted calibrator; identity passthrough when absent.\"\"\"\n","    if calibrator is None:\n","        return probs\n","    return np.clip(calibrator.predict(probs), 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n","\n","\n","def train_multiseed(Z_fit, agg_fit, y_fit, Z_stop, agg_stop, y_stop,\n","                    Z_score, agg_score, label: str = \"\", n_seeds: int | None = None):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Train N_SEEDS models and return seed-averaged scores plus the noise floor.\n","\n","    A single neural run cannot support a confirmatory claim about a ~0.005-0.01\n","    AP effect. Averaging reduces variance in the reported score, and the returned\n","    per-seed inner APs quantify how much of any observed delta could be seed\n","    noise alone.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    n_seeds = CONFIG[\"N_SEEDS\"] if n_seeds is None else n_seeds\n","    score_stack, stop_stack, epochs, inner_aps = [], [], [], []\n","\n","    for k in range(n_seeds):\n","        seed = CONFIG[\"SEED\"] + 1000 * k\n","        model, best_ep, best_ap = train_one_model(\n","            Z_fit, agg_fit, y_fit, Z_stop, agg_stop, y_stop, seed, f\"{label}/s{k}\"\n","        )\n","        score_stack.append(infer(model, Z_score, agg_score))\n","        stop_stack.append(infer(model, Z_stop, agg_stop))\n","        epochs.append(best_ep)\n","        inner_aps.append(best_ap)\n","        del model\n","\n","    probs_score = np.mean(np.vstack(score_stack), axis=0).astype(np.float32)\n","    probs_stop = np.mean(np.vstack(stop_stack), axis=0).astype(np.float32)\n","    calibrator = fit_calibrator(probs_stop, y_stop)\n","\n","    info = {\n","        \"n_seeds\": n_seeds,\n","        \"best_epochs\": epochs,\n","        \"inner_ap_mean\": float(np.mean(inner_aps)),\n","        \"inner_ap_std\": float(np.std(inner_aps, ddof=1)) if n_seeds > 1 else 0.0,\n","    }\n","    print(f\"      {label}: seeds {n_seeds} | epochs {epochs} | \"\n","          f\"inner AP {info['inner_ap_mean']:.4f} +/- {info['inner_ap_std']:.4f}\")\n","    return probs_score, calibrator, info"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"id":"26e587fd","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.386503Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.386177Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-01T03:14:29.009107Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-01T03:14:29.008199Z"},"papermill":{"duration":35.633838,"end_time":"2026-10-01T03:14:29.015113+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-01T03:13:53.381275+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[1] Resolving environment and loading raw data...\n","    Data directory: /kaggle/input/competitions/ieee-fraud-detection | Device: cuda\n","    Joining train_identity.csv via left join...\n","    Memory downcast [raw]: 1955.4 MB -> 1044.7 MB (46.6% saved)\n","[2] Enforcing deterministic chronological sort and block construction...\n","    Block 5 OOT quarantine: PASSED (sealed; scored later, never trained on).\n","    Block profile (prevalence drift check):\n","                rows  fraud_rate  first_day  last_day\n","chrono_block                                         \n","1             118108    0.023927          0        25\n","2             118108    0.040065         25        63\n","3             118108    0.037508         63       100\n","4             118108    0.039041        100       140\n","5             118108    0.034409        140       181\n"]}],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 6. Data Ingestion & Temporal Structuring\n","# ==============================================================================\n","print(\"[1] Resolving environment and loading raw data...\")\n","data_dir = resolve_path(CONFIG[\"CANDIDATE_DATA_DIRS\"])\n","print(f\"    Data directory: {data_dir} | Device: {DEVICE}\")\n","\n","transaction_path = os.path.join(data_dir, \"train_transaction.csv\")\n","trans_df = pd.read_csv(transaction_path)\n","record_input_artifact(\"train_transaction\", transaction_path)\n","id_path = os.path.join(data_dir, \"train_identity.csv\")\n","\n","if os.path.exists(id_path):\n","    print(\"    Joining train_identity.csv via left join...\")\n","    id_df = pd.read_csv(id_path)\n","    record_input_artifact(\"train_identity\", id_path, optional=True)\n","    df = trans_df.merge(id_df, on=CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"], how=\"left\")\n","    del id_df\n","else:\n","    print(\"    WARNING: train_identity.csv not found. Transaction columns only.\")\n","    record_input_artifact(\"train_identity\", id_path, optional=True)\n","    df = trans_df.copy()\n","\n","del trans_df\n","gc.collect()\n","\n","assert df[CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"]].is_unique, \"Fatal: duplicate TransactionIDs post-merge.\"\n","assert df[CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]].notna().all(), \"Fatal: null TransactionDT.\"\n","assert df[CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]].notna().all(), \"Fatal: null isFraud.\"\n","assert set(df[CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]].unique()) <= {0, 1}, \"Fatal: target not binary.\"\n","\n","df = reduce_memory(df, \"raw\")\n","\n","print(\"[2] Enforcing deterministic chronological sort and block construction...\")\n","df = df.sort_values([CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"], CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"]],\n","                    kind=\"mergesort\").reset_index(drop=True)\n","\n","assert df[CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]].is_monotonic_increasing, (\n","    \"Fatal: frame is not chronologically sorted; every causal-predecessor edge \"\n","    \"would silently become 